:"see also","value_wikitext":"","value_text":"","links":[]},{"name":"previous","value_wikitext":"[[The Bulls of Pamplona]]","value_text":"The Bulls of Pamplona","links":[{"target_title":"The Bulls of Pamplona","label":"The Bulls of Pamplona","target_id":"huntik:page:12978","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Bulls_of_Pamplona","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A12978"}]},{"name":"next","value_wikitext":"[[The Guardian of Yonaguni]]","value_text":"The Guardian of Yonaguni","links":[{"target_title":"The Guardian of Yonaguni","label":"The Guardian of Yonaguni","target_id":"huntik:page:18095","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Guardian_of_Yonaguni","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A18095"}]}],"start":0,"end":699}],"sections":[{"heading":"Synopsis","level":2,"wikitext":"The Huntik team launched an attack on [[Dr. Benway]], but in the confrontation both [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] were sent back in time by the [[Legendary Titan]] of time, [[Kronos]].","text":"The Huntik team launched an attack on Dr. Benway, but in the confrontation both Lok Lambert and Sophie Casterwill were sent back in time by the Legendary Titan of time, Kronos."},{"heading":"Trivia","level":2,"wikitext":"*During the first battle in the story, there was originally some pages where Kronos fought and defeated both [[Sabriel]] and [[Baselaird]], but these had to be scrapped as this comic was set during Season 2 and the Titans has not be illustrated in their Powerbonded forms. \n*The original cover featuring [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Kronos]] was changed shortly before the magazine's release so that it would promote the new second season that had begun airing. The new cover features [[Venomaster]] who does not appear in the story. \n\n[[Category:Comics| 17]]\n\n{{Clear}}{{ComicsNav}}","text":"*During the first battle in the story, there was originally some pages where Kronos fought and defeated both Sabriel and Baselaird, but these had to be scrapped as this comic was set during Season 2 and the Titans has not be illustrated in their Powerbonded forms. \n*The original cover featuring Lok Lambert and Kronos was changed shortly before the magazine's release so that it would promote the new second season that had begun airing. The new cover features Venomaster who does not appear in the story."}],"full_text":"The Power of Kronos is the seventeenth issue of the Huntik Magazine comic series and the penultimate comic to be released. The story takes place during the second season.\n== Synopsis ==\nThe Huntik team launched an attack on Dr. Benway, but in the confrontation both Lok Lambert and Sophie Casterwill were sent back in time by the Legendary Titan of time, Kronos.\n\n== Trivia ==\n*During the first battle in the story, there was originally some pages where Kronos fought and defeated both Sabriel and Baselaird, but these had to be scrapped as this comic was set during Season 2 and the Titans has not be illustrated in their Powerbonded forms. \n*The original cover featuring Lok Lambert and Kronos was changed shortly before the magazine's release so that it would promote the new second season that had begun airing. The new cover features Venomaster who does not appear in the story.","raw_wikitext":"{{infobox comic\n| issue             = 17\n| image             = <tabber>Final Cover=[[File:Comic_17_cover.png|250px]]|-|Original Cover=[[File:Comic 17 lost cover.jpg|250px]]</tabber>\n| released          = November 2011\n| writer            = Nicola Venanzetti\n| artist            = Davide Cencini\n| italian           = Il Potere di Kronos\n| mission           = \n| new characters    = [[Nostradamus]] <br> [[Viktor Casterwill]]\n| new titans        = [[Kronos]]\n| new powerbondings = \n| new spells        = \n| new items         = \n| new locations     = [[Prague, Czech Republic]]\n| see also          =\n| previous          = [[The Bulls of Pamplona]]\n| next              = [[The Guardian of Yonaguni]]\n}}'''The Power of Kronos''' is the seventeenth issue of the ''[[Huntik Magazine]]'' comic series and the penultimate comic to be released. The story takes place during the [[Season 2|second season]].\n== Synopsis ==\nThe Huntik team launched an attack on [[Dr. Benway]], but in the confrontation both [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] were sent back in time by the [[Legendary Titan]] of time, [[Kronos]].\n\n== Trivia ==\n*During the first battle in the story, there was originally some pages where Kronos fought and defeated both [[Sabriel]] and [[Baselaird]], but these had to be scrapped as this comic was set during Season 2 and the Titans has not be illustrated in their Powerbonded forms. \n*The original cover featuring [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Kronos]] was changed shortly before the magazine's release so that it would promote the new second season that had begun airing. The new cover features [[Venomaster]] who does not appear in the story. \n\n[[Category:Comics| 17]]\n\n{{Clear}}{{ComicsNav}}","categories":["Comics"],"links":[{"target_title":"File:Comic 17 cover.png","label":"250px","target_id":null,"target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/File:Comic_17_cover.png","status":"file_reference"},{"target_title":"File:Comic 17 lost cover.jpg","label":"250px","target_id":null,"target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/File:Comic_17_lost_cover.jpg","status":"file_reference"},{"target_title":"Nostradamus","label":"Nostradamus","target_id":"huntik:page:6911","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Nostradamus","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A6911"},{"target_title":"Viktor Casterwill","label":"Viktor Casterwill","target_id":"huntik:page:12973","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Viktor_Casterwill","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A12973"},{"target_title":"Kronos","label":"Kronos","target_id":"huntik:page:8643","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Kronos","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A